# AUTORUN: copy to the drive as /AUTORUN (no extension) and it runs at
# start-up, a line at a time, as if typed at the prompt. Lines starting
# with # or REM are comments; @ before a command (or "echo off") stops it
# being shown. Esc during start-up skips it; Esc while it runs stops it.
# "run /AUTORUN" runs it again by hand.

# Wait for WiFi (up to 20 s), then put a Windows or Samba share at /NET.
# The login comes from /SMB/CREDS: mount the share once by hand and answer
# yes to saving the login. At start-up mount never stops to ask.
wifi wait 20
# mount //mypc/share /NET

# Anything else, e.g. start in a folder:
# cd /EXAMPLES
